# Component 2 — PV-Aware, Polarity-Aware, Bridge-Resilient Graph Reasoner (Standalone Explanation)

> **Audience:** someone who has never seen this project before.  
> **Goal:** after reading this document, an outsider should understand:
> 1) what Component 2 is solving,  
> 2) what it consumes/produces,  
> 3) how it works step-by-step,  
> 4) why “partial/bridge evidence” won’t get suppressed,  
> 5) how we evaluate it rigorously.

---

## 0) One-paragraph story

Component 1 already **scores and partitions evidence** for each claim using NLI-based Premise Validation (PV) and evidence management boxes **A/S/C**.  
Component 2 is the first component that **actually reasons** over that evidence as a graph. It runs a **PV-aware GNN** (soft masking, not pruning), separates **support vs refute** evidence with polarity-aware aggregation, and **rescues crucial low-PV “bridge” edges** using a bridge/path structural score. If diagnostics (ESI/RPI) say evidence is insufficient, it can do a **single recovery step** by moving the most promising bridge edges from **S → A** and re-reason once. Finally, because FactKG is binary, insufficiency is handled via **selective prediction (abstention)** and evaluated with **risk–coverage** curves.

